  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry forecast holds for next 5-6 days\n\nFreeze seems likely enough to post yet another freeze warning\nfor the two counties not yet out of the growing season. While\nthe urban places may stay above freezing, the light wind and few\nclouds will help the rural areas to get down to 32F. Guidance\ndoes keep the values up more 32-34F for most places, but the\nwind should be gone, and they just need an hour to drop enough\nto warrant the freeze warning for >50% of each county. \n\nThe high pressure making the light/nil wind and mainly clear \nsky possible will silently hold onto the region for many more \ndays. A front, starved of moisture, will approach from the Upper\nGreat Lakes Mon night-Tues, but PoPs are hardly worth having as\nPWATs stay very low before the arrival of the baroclinic zone. A\nnew airmass, just as dry as this one then moves in from the NW\nand continues the dry forecast. Per almost every\nmodel/member/wooly worm I could find, the next chance for rain \ncomes on/near Halloween.",
